                     <title ref="LIT0049IHA#s22IHA"/>
                     <incipit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#1v">-1v</locus>سورة بني اسرايل ماية وعشرون اىة مكية \ بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم , سُبْحَانَ الّذِيْ اَسْرَىْ بِعَبْدِهِ لَيلاً مِنَ المَسْجِدِ الحَرَامِ , اِلَىْ المَسْجِدِ الأَقْصَا</incipit>
                     <explicit xml:lang="ar">
                        <locus target="#16v">-16v</locus>قَالَ اَقتَلتَ نَفْساً زَاِكِيَةَ (هكذا) بِغَيْرِ نَفْسٍ لّقَدْ جِئتَ شَيْأً نُّكْراً<note>جِئتَ :  
diacritics of yā' below hamza.</note>
                     </explicit>
                     <note>17:1-18:74. Title of suras rubricated. Three dots as verse markers, but irregular, added probably at a second phase. Some rubricated words (takbīr, 14v, 16r). End of the ǧuz’ by another hand (16r-16v). Two black ovals with a red dot in the middle, mark the end of the ǧuz’. Twelve lines a page. Short vowels with a thinner qalam. In the margins, mark of ǧuz’ and ḥizb in red, corrections by another hand (8r, 9r, forgotten words), and taṣdīq closing the ǧuz’ (16v).</note>
                     <note/>
